    "q-352684": {
      "dom_id": "step-q352684",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "$$\n\nEvaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x{sech}^{3}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "$$\n\nFirst, we find the hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the trigonometric identity \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sec}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}.\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, the corresponding hyperbolic identity is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sech}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x}.\n$$\n\nNow, we rewrite the integral using the above identity, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x{sech}^{3}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x\\cdot {(\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x})}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\frac{1}{{cosh}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}{sech}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x\\,{|}_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{tanh}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)-\\operatorname{tanh}⁡0 \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}-{e}^{-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}}{{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}+{e}^{-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}}-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{2-{2}^{-1}}{2+{2}^{-1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2-\\frac{1}{2}}{2+\\frac{1}{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\frac{3}{2}}{\\frac{5}{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "field-1",
          "type": "blank",
          "dom_id": "freeResponseTextbox-1",
