    "q-352673": {
      "dom_id": "step-q352673",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "$$\n\nEvaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\operatorname{coth}⁡x\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x\\operatorname{sech}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "$$\n\nFirst, we find the hyperbolic identities corresponding to the trigonometric identities \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\,\\text{ and }\\,\\operatorname{sec}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}.\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, the corresponding hyperbolic identities are\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{coth}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x}\\,\\text{ and }\\,\\operatorname{sech}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x}.\n$$\n\nNow, we rewrite the integral using the above identities, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\operatorname{coth}⁡x\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x\\operatorname{sech}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\frac{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x}\\cdot \\operatorname{sinh}⁡x\\cdot \\operatorname{cosh}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x\\,{|}_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)-\\operatorname{sinh}⁡0 \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}-{e}^{-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}}{2}-\\frac{{e}^{0}-{e}^{-0}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{2-{2}^{-1}}{2}-\\frac{1-1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{3}{2})}{2}-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
