    "q-352678": {
      "dom_id": "step-q352678",
      "name": "Question 10",
      "problem": "$$\n\nEvaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\operatorname{coth}⁡x\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x\\operatorname{sech}⁡x\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "$$\n\nFirst, we recall the following  identities:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{coth}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x},\\,\\operatorname{sech}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x}\n$$\n\nNow, we rewrite the integral using the above identities, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\operatorname{coth}⁡x\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x\\operatorname{sech}⁡x\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\frac{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x}\\cdot \\operatorname{sinh}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x}\\cdot \\operatorname{cosh}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x\\,{|}_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡3)-\\operatorname{sinh}⁡0 \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}-{e}^{-\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}}{2}-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{3-{3}^{-1}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{8}{3})}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
