    "q-352935": {
      "dom_id": "step-q352935",
      "name": "Question 11",
      "problem": "$$\n\nEvaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1/2)}^{0}\\frac{\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x}{{cosh}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "$$\n\n$$\n\nFirst, we write the integral as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1/2)}^{0}\\frac{\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x}{{cosh}^{2}⁡x}\\text{d}x={\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1/2)}^{0}\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{1}{{cosh}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nNow we find the hyperbolic identities corresponding to the trigonometric identities \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sec}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\text{ and }\\,\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}.\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, the corresponding hyperbolic identities are\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sech}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x}\\,\\text{ and }\\,\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x}.\n$$\n\nThen, we use the above identities to write the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1/2)}^{0}\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{1}{{cosh}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1/2)}^{0}\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x\\cdot {sech}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}{sech}^{2}⁡x{|}_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1/2)}^{0} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}{sech}^{2}⁡(0)+\\frac{1}{2}{sech}^{2}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡1/2) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{4}{({e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡1/2}+{e}^{-\\operatorname{ln}⁡1/2})^{2}}-\\frac{4}{({e}^{0}+{e}^{0})^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{(1/2+2)^{2}}-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{9}{50}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
