    "q-96263": {
      "dom_id": "step-q96263",
      "name": "Question 13",
      "problem": "$\\int \\frac{5\\operatorname{coth}⁡x-3\\operatorname{csch}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=$",
      "worked_solution": "$$\n\n$$\n\nFirst, we write the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{5\\operatorname{coth}⁡x-3\\operatorname{csch}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x}(5\\operatorname{coth}⁡x-3\\operatorname{csch}⁡x)\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nNow, recall the following identity:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{csch}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x}\n$$\n\nThen, we use the above identity to express the integral as\n\n$$\n\\int \\operatorname{csch}⁡x(5\\operatorname{coth}⁡x-3\\operatorname{csch}⁡x)\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{5\\operatorname{coth}⁡x-3\\operatorname{csch}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\operatorname{csch}⁡x(5\\operatorname{coth}⁡x-3\\operatorname{csch}⁡x)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5\\int \\operatorname{coth}⁡x\\operatorname{csch}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x-3\\int {csch}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-5\\operatorname{csch}⁡x+3\\operatorname{coth}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
