    "q-352916": {
      "dom_id": "step-q352916",
      "name": "Question 15",
      "problem": "$$\n\nEvaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\frac{{tanh}^{2}⁡x}{2{sinh}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "$$\n\n$$\n\nFirst, we write the integral as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\frac{{tanh}^{2}⁡x}{2{sinh}^{2}⁡x}\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\frac{1}{{sinh}^{2}⁡x}\\cdot {tanh}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nNow we need to find the hyperbolic identity that corresponds to the trigonometric identity \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}.\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, the corresponding hyperbolic identity is\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x}{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x}.\n$$\n\nThen, we use the above identity to write the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\frac{1}{{sinh}^{2}⁡x}\\cdot {tanh}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\frac{1}{{sinh}^{2}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{{sinh}^{2}⁡x}{{cosh}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\frac{{sinh}^{2}⁡x}{{sinh}^{2}⁡x}\\cdot \\frac{1}{{cosh}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\frac{1}{{cosh}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}{sech}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x{|}_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{tanh}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡3)-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{tanh}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{{e}^{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}-1}{{e}^{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}+1}-\\frac{{e}^{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}-1}{{e}^{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}+1}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{4}{5}-\\frac{3}{5}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
