    "q-352968": {
      "dom_id": "step-q352968",
      "name": "Question 16",
      "problem": "$$\n\nEvaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\frac{\\operatorname{coth}⁡x}{{csch}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "$$\n\nFirst, we find the hyperbolic identities that correspond to the following trigonometric identities:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x},\\,\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, the corresponding hyperbolic identities are\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{coth}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x},\\,\\operatorname{csch}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x}.\n$$\n\nNow, we rewrite the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\frac{\\operatorname{coth}⁡x}{{csch}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\operatorname{coth}⁡x\\cdot \\frac{1}{{csch}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\frac{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x}\\cdot {sinh}^{2}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this by substitution. Let $u=\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x.$ Then,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nNow, we fill the table for the limits of integration, according to the rule $u=\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\operatorname{ln}⁡3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $1$ | $\\frac{5}{3}$ |\n\nNow, we evaluate the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡3}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{5/3}u\\,\\cdot \\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{{u}^{2}}{2}{|}_{1}^{5/3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}({(\\frac{5}{3})}^{2}-{1}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{25}{9}-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{9}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
