    "q-352966": {
      "dom_id": "step-q352966",
      "name": "Question 17",
      "problem": "$$\n\nEvaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}2\\operatorname{csch}⁡(2x)\\operatorname{coth}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "$$\n\nFirst, we find the hyperbolic identities that correspond to the following trigonometric identities:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x},\\,\\operatorname{csc}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\n$$\n\nUsing Osborn's rule, the corresponding hyperbolic identities are\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{coth}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x},\\,\\operatorname{csch}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sinh}⁡x}.\n$$\n\nNow, we rewrite the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}2\\operatorname{csch}⁡(2x)\\operatorname{coth}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x & =2{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}\\operatorname{csch}⁡(2x)\\operatorname{coth}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2x)}\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2x)}{\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2x)}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this by substitution. Let $u=2x.$ Then,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}u=2\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nNow, we fill the table for the limits of integration, according to the rule $u=2x.$\n\n| $x$ | $\\operatorname{ln}⁡2$ | $\\operatorname{ln}⁡4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $\\operatorname{ln}⁡4$ | $\\operatorname{ln}⁡16$ |\n\nNow, we evaluate the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}2{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}\\operatorname{csch}⁡(2x)\\operatorname{coth}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡16}\\operatorname{csch}⁡(u)\\operatorname{coth}⁡(u)\\,\\cdot \\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{csch}⁡(u){|}_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡4}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡16} \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{csch}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡16)+\\operatorname{csch}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡4) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡16)}+\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡4)} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{(\\frac{16-{16}^{-1}}{2})}+\\frac{1}{(\\frac{4-{4}^{-1}}{2})} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{(\\frac{255}{32})}+\\frac{1}{(\\frac{15}{8})} \\\\  & =\\frac{104}{255}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
